{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>When you go out as a camp, etc.</b> That is, although there are finer points of transgression for which HaShem will not punish, and if He does punish it will be a light punishment, the verse informs us that at a time of danger — which is when they go out against their enemies — they require guarding from every fine point of transgression, as it says, <b>from every evil thing</b>, etc. And He included in the word <b>thing</b> also causes from which evil may ensue. And He drew attention through what He commanded adjacent to this: ״כִּי יִהְיֶה בְךָ אִישׁ אֲשֶׁר לֹא יִהְיֶה טָהוֹר״ and so forth, and our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Ketuvot 46a) that contemplations of transgression by day bring about a nocturnal emission at night, and the verse intended this adjacency to teach that regarding such a matter He commands with the statement ״וְנִשְׁמַרְתָּ מִכֹּל״ etc."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:18:45.058156208Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}